# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the cuda-dev and cuda12-dev test presets.
#
# WSL's CUDA driver shim leaks 320 bytes in 2 allocations, once per process,
# from a pthread_once initializer reached through cuGetProcAddress_v2 /
# cuDriverGetVersion. No MENOS frame appears in the stack, and it happens with
# both the CUDA 12.4 and 13.3 runtimes (docs/adr/0014 section 17).
#
# The pattern is the WSL shim's full path, deliberately: a leak through a
# native Linux libcuda, or any leak whose stack does not pass through this
# library, is still reported. LeakSanitizer prints every suppressed leak in
# its summary, so this never hides that the suppression fired.
leak:/usr/lib/wsl/lib/libcuda.so
